  "releaseNotes": "- Changes to support loading a container from IoC.Configuration file concurrently in multiple threads.\n\t\t\t- Added a new element 'providedValue' to support injecting values into constructors and properties using values generated by application\n\t\t\tvia setting a value of optional (nullable) property 'ValueProviders' in 'IoC.Configuration.DiContainerBuilder.FileBased.FileBasedConfigurationParameters' when loading the configuration from IoC.Configuration file.\n\t\t\tValueProviders is a collection of 'IoC.Configuration.IValueProvider' that has a method to return value provided (generated) during dependency injection.\n\t\t\tThis might be helpful in some scenarios. For example application might create a Serilog or Log4Net logger on startup, and we might want\n\t\t\tto pass the logger as a provided value to an IoC.Configuration module as well as to native (Autofac, Nnject, etc.) module when setting up dependency injection using IoC.Configuration.\n\t\t\tSee the IoC.Configuration file at https://github.com/artakhak/IoC.Configuration/blob/master/IoC.Configuration.Tests/IoCConfiguration_providedValue.xml and\n\t\t\ttests in the following directory for examples:\n\t\t\thttps://github.com/artakhak/IoC.Configuration/tree/master/IoC.Configuration.Tests/ProvidedValue",
